Remove the unused Chrome launcher from glide/computer/browser/cdp.py (finding 8, guards-dispatch).

Owner: whoever owns cdp.py. Apply from the repository root with `git apply docs/notes/cdp-launcher-removal.patch`,
then delete the TODO entry for cdp.py in `ALLOWED` in tests/test_process_seams.py (the test only warns until you do).

What goes: CHROME_CANDIDATES, DEFAULT_PROFILE, find_chrome, free_port and `class Chrome` (about 110 lines, the one
production `subprocess.Popen` outside the spawn seam), and the imports only they used (shutil, socket, subprocess,
tempfile, pathlib.Path). What stays: CDPError, local_debugger_url, _traced, _get_json and Session, which
execution/dom.py and execution/playwright_cli.py import.

Nothing in glide/ calls the launcher (tests/test_process_seams.py::test_nothing_in_glide_reaches_the_chrome_launcher).
Only two test files named it: tests/conftest.py (the `find_chrome` guard, which has nothing left to guard; the
`subprocess.Popen` refusal beside it stays) and tests/test_no_real_machine.py (two parametrized touches). Removing a
guard from a function that no longer exists does not weaken the guard.

